{
  "id": "a1-022-demonstrative-pronouns",
  "level": "A1",
  "focusArea": "cases",
  "title": "Demonstrative Pronouns",
  "titleRussian": "Указательные местоимения",
  "description": "Demonstrative pronouns: this/these and that/those",
  "descriptionRussian": "Указательные местоимения: этот/эти и тот/те",
  "imageName": "hand.point.right.fill",
  "intro": "Demonstrative pronouns point to specific things - 'this book' or 'that house.' Russian has two sets: этот/эта/это/эти (this/these - closer) and тот/та/то/те (that/those - farther). Like adjectives, they must agree in gender and number with the noun. There's also a special use: Это alone can mean 'this is' for any gender.",
  "rules": [
    "Этот (m), эта (f), это (n), эти (pl) = this/these - for things nearby or just mentioned.",
    "Тот (m), та (f), то (n), те (pl) = that/those - for things farther away or previously mentioned.",
    "Demonstratives agree in gender and number: этот дом (m), эта книга (f), это окно (n), эти люди (pl).",
    "Это (standalone) = 'this is' for ANY gender: Это книга. Это дом. Это окно. (This is a book/house/window.)"
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Этот дом большой. (This house is big.), этот for masculine",
    "Эта книга интересная. (This book is interesting.), эта for feminine",
    "Это письмо важное. (This letter is important.), это for neuter",
    "Эти студенты умные. (These students are smart.), эти for plural",
    "Тот человек — мой друг. (That person is my friend.), тот for distant masculine",
    "Это моя мама. (This is my mom.), Это as 'this is'"
  ],
